            "lean": "Samplinglib abstracts only the properties consumed by the proof: real-linearity, pointwise order preservation, continuity, and the exact one-sided derivative identity."
          }
        ]
      },
      "graph_node": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.StochasticProcesses.backwardInterpolation_contraction_of_expandedBakryEmery",
      "reconstruction": {
        "text": "Let X be an arbitrary type, let L : (X → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (X → ℝ) be a real-linear generator, and let α ∈ ℝ with α > 0. Assume that for every g : X → ℝ and y ∈ X, α Γ_L(g,g)(y) ≤ (1/2)(L(Γ_L(g,g))(y) - Γ_L(g,Lg)(y) - Γ_L(g,Lg)(y)). Let P_u : (X → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (X → ℝ), indexed by u ∈ ℝ, be order preserving: whenever f(y) ≤ g(y) for every y ∈ X, P_u f(z) ≤ P_u g(z) for every z ∈ X. Let h_u : X → ℝ be an orbit indexed by u ∈ ℝ, fix x ∈ X, and define Φ(u) = P_u(Γ_L(h_u,h_u))(x). Assume Φ is continuous on ℝ and that, for every u ∈ ℝ, its right-sided derivative at u within [u,∞) is exactly P_u(L(Γ_L(h_u,h_u)) - 2Γ_L(h_u,Lh_u))(x). Then, for every s,t ∈ ℝ with s ≤ t, P_s(Γ_L(h_s,h_s))(x) ≤ P_t(Γ_L(h_t,h_t))(x) exp(-(2α)(t-s)).",
